**********Web Search Result**********

The GitHub repository for SNLI-VE provides detailed information on the dataset's creation and its relationship to NLI datasets. SNLI-VE is built on top of SNLI and Flickr30K, aiming to solve the Visual Entailment (VE) task by reasoning about the relationship between an image premise and a text hypothesis. The dataset was generated using the `snli_ve_generator.py` script, which creates the SNLI-VE dataset in `train`, `dev`, and `test` splits with disjoint image sets. Each entry contains a `Flickr30kID` field to associate with the original Flickr30K image ID. ([github.com](https://github.com/necla-ml/SNLI-VE?utm_source=openai))

Additionally, the paper "Dataset Creation for Visual Entailment using Generative AI" discusses the creation of a synthetic dataset for training visual entailment models. It mentions that existing datasets for visual entailment are small and sparse compared to datasets for textual entailment. The authors base their synthetic dataset on the SNLI dataset for textual entailment, taking the premise text from SNLI as input prompts in a generative image model to create corresponding images. ([arxiv.org](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.11605?utm_source=openai))

Furthermore, the paper "Building a Vietnamese Dataset for Natural Language Inference Models" provides insights into the creation methods of NLI datasets like SICK and SNLI. It outlines the three-step process used in creating these datasets: sentence selection, sentence generation (manually or automatically generating entailment, contradiction, and neutral sentences), and sample generation (collecting judgments from workers to determine the final relations of premise-hypothesis pairs). ([ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9311348/?utm_source=openai))

These sources collectively provide comprehensive information on existing VE datasets, their basis on NLI datasets, and the creation processes of SNLI-VE and SICK-VTE datasets.  No source extracted due to invalid syntax

